{
  "inShort": "No playable build or test findings can be opened, so the team finished behind: the checkpoint goal was missed. Sprint 4 claimed a build and polish, but showed a mountain photograph and a film reference. What actually got done remains unknown; two-island travel, the tide loop, co-op sailing and five-player testing remain unverified.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyivb01awtvz8v6fyg2xh",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is complete. The inspected repository supplies demo projects, an MIT license and import instructions. It does not show this game's playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj2j01axtvz8lc3mdzjj",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains complete. The title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny, but the video was not watched. This establishes a reference, not a verified choice of style for the game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj5x01aytvz8lsr5pz2m",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is complete. The inspected Wikipedia article matches that promise. It supplies guidance, not findings from the five-player test."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj7c01aztvz8t0jcex56",
      "text": "A private design board for the team remains complete. Its contents were not inspected, so it cannot establish what the prototype demonstrates."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj7w01b0tvz86u0a9ezv",
      "text": "A storyboard for the trailer was cut from the plan. It is not an outstanding obligation."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The mountain photograph is outside the planned tasks. It shows no game scene and does not demonstrate the tide loop."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What did the five players establish about island travel, tide clarity and sailing together?",
    "Which parts of the playable slice remain untested?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlogs #1–#4 reported tide changes, co-op sailing, a second island, testing and a build; each received 0 applause and 0 views, and no playable or store link is listed.",
    "team": "The stated 40–60 hours cover Alex only; four weeks of confirmed work have not produced an inspectable slice. Mia stopped confirming after week 1, so her contribution to sailing and testing cannot be counted.",
    "management": "The completed tasks supply references and a board, not the playable evidence needed to connect this checkpoint to release; publishing the prototype devlog nevertheless meets the stage's sole required task. At the next checkpoint, attach the two-island build and five-player findings, including what remains untested."
  }
}

